<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Intl Comml Bank to sell U.S. bank stake.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Intl Comml Bank to sell U.S. bank stake.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's International Commercial Bank of China said it has decided to sell 209,988 shares in a U.S. bank for US$40 million to comply with a U.S. Federal Reserve ruling.</p>
<p>The International Commercial Bank of China said its board of directors had agreed to sell the company's shares in the Chinese American Bank of New York to Taiwan's Chinfon Group.</p>
<p>As of June 30, the Chinese American Bank's net asset value was at $79.735 million, with the International Commercial Bank of China holding 93.328 percent of the stake.</p>
</text>
